- And what are we stopping here for?

00:36:50.590 --> 00:36:52.970
- El caballo no puede estar aquí toda la noche.

00:36:52.970 --> 00:36:53.810
- What was that?

00:36:53.810 --> 00:36:56.960
- The horse is tired.

00:36:56.960 --> 00:36:58.320
- Take us back to the boat.

00:37:01.370 --> 00:37:03.130
Did you hear me? Take us back to the boat.

00:37:03.130 --> 00:37:05.410
I already told you the horse is tired.

00:37:05.410 --> 00:37:16.030
Chuck, let's get out.

00:37:16.030 --> 00:37:23.640
Say, uh, our boat leaves in an hour for South America.

00:37:23.640 --> 00:37:25.720
How much of a walk is near the docks?

00:37:25.720 --> 00:37:27.440
Yo no entiendo bien ingles.

00:37:27.440 --> 00:37:28.360
Vamos, Pancho!

00:37:33.230 --> 00:37:34.230
What did he say?

00:37:34.230 --> 00:37:39.360
Something about not understanding English.

00:37:39.360 --> 00:37:41.820
He must not understand money either.

00:37:41.820 --> 00:37:44.460
He didn't take his fare.

00:37:44.460 --> 00:37:49.720
Chuck, what do we do now?

00:37:49.720 --> 00:37:50.710
I don't know.

00:37:50.710 --> 00:37:57.550
Uh, let's get a drink.

00:38:00.120 --> 00:38:06.910
No, wait a minute. We should go back to the boat.

00:38:06.910 --> 00:38:09.430
Close it, Fred, now.

00:38:34.830 --> 00:38:35.670
Feel scared?

00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:54.390
- That's game eight here.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:00.450
Mm-hmm.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:31.660
don't care what happens now.

00:41:32.440 --> 00:41:33.880
I just don't care.

00:41:34.060 --> 00:41:36.960
Laura, don't keep saying that. Please don't keep saying.

00:41:37.950 --> 00:41:41.030
I won't. I won't

00:41:41.030 --> 00:41:44.020
say it anymore. Because I do.

00:41:44.020 --> 00:41:46.480
Oh,

00:42:01.530 --> 00:42:04.400
- Lala.

00:42:04.400 --> 00:42:06.460
- Lala?

00:42:06.460 --> 00:42:09.710
- Lala.

00:42:09.710 --> 00:42:10.400
- Lala?

00:42:50.670 --> 00:43:00.000
car knife wound no other marks we're waiting mr.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:30.000
Oh can I make you understand you've got the wrong man. I loved her. You loved her so you killed her. That's understandable. She was all I had. So you made sure no one could take her from you. Oh you're blind. Why would we come all this way together? I let you tell me why. Just understand.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:34.450
three questions. How long had this woman been in Havana?

00:43:34.450 --> 00:43:42.620
Oh, we got off the boat around six o'clock, see.

00:43:42.620 --> 00:43:46.710
Eight hours ago. Had she ever been here before?

00:43:46.710 --> 00:43:47.760
No.

00:43:47.760 --> 00:43:49.890
Did she know anyone here? Anyone at all?

00:43:49.890 --> 00:43:51.040
No.

00:43:51.040 --> 00:43:52.340
There is your answer.

00:43:52.340 --> 00:43:55.350
Do you still insist somebody else did it?

00:43:55.350 --> 00:43:57.180
In a place where she had just arrived?

00:43:57.180 --> 00:43:59.540
In a place where she had never been in her life before?

00:44:00.220 --> 00:44:01.620
And above all, with your own knife.

00:44:02.080 --> 00:44:03.360
It wasn't my knife.

00:44:03.460 --> 00:44:05.140
But you just admitted a moment ago, it was your...

00:44:05.140 --> 00:44:06.380
I didn't admit it wasn't my knife.

00:44:06.440 --> 00:44:07.940
I merely said it looked like my knife, but it wasn't.

00:44:08.200 --> 00:44:08.800
Oh, yes.

00:44:09.550 --> 00:44:10.530
Now I remember.

00:44:11.650 --> 00:44:12.610
The knife you bought.

00:44:13.290 --> 00:44:14.290
You did buy a knife.

00:44:14.510 --> 00:44:15.550
Yes, I bought a knife!

00:44:15.880 --> 00:44:17.440
Save your strength, my friend.

00:44:17.540 --> 00:44:18.220
You may need it.

00:44:23.950 --> 00:44:24.610
Your knife.

00:44:26.080 --> 00:44:26.840
Let me see.

00:44:28.930 --> 00:44:30.000
Describe it again, please.

00:44:34.800 --> 00:44:38.700
On the handle of the knife I had, the little carved monkey was holding his ears.

00:44:41.010 --> 00:44:43.410
The knife you've got is covering his eyes. You can see that.

00:44:43.570 --> 00:44:45.630
He's covering his eyes, but not mine.

00:44:46.330 --> 00:44:48.960
Don't joke. If you don't believe me, ask the shopkeeper.

00:44:49.100 --> 00:44:50.540
Find out what kind of a knife I bought.

00:44:54.330 --> 00:45:00.000
Are you sure?

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.460
- Are you sure this is the place?

00:45:02.460 --> 00:45:05.340
- Yeah, yeah, that's it.

00:45:05.340 --> 00:45:07.200
- I repeat, for a stranger in Havana,

00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:09.300
you certainly found an out-of-the-way place

00:45:09.300 --> 00:45:10.780
in a very much of a hurry.

00:45:10.780 --> 00:45:12.860
- We didn't find it.

00:45:12.860 --> 00:45:14.620
I told you a guide brought us here.

00:45:14.620 --> 00:45:16.900
- I know, a guide who kept pestering.

00:45:16.900 --> 00:45:19.250
You're the one who drove you to the nightclub, huh?

00:45:19.250 --> 00:45:21.380
- You don't believe anything, do you?

00:45:21.380 --> 00:45:28.640
- My clients have a chronic tendency to color the truth.

00:45:28.640 --> 00:45:29.920
You first, Mr. Scott.

00:45:37.930 --> 00:45:39.760
For a moment, please. Not so quick.

00:45:39.760 --> 00:45:54.590
I'm Kim.

00:45:54.590 --> 00:45:57.650
I'm Lieutenant Acosta, Homicide Squad.

00:46:01.600 --> 00:46:04.500
- What can I do for you? - Madam, would you please tell the gentleman...

00:46:04.500 --> 00:46:05.800
We'll ask the question.

00:46:05.800 --> 00:46:11.040
Take a look at this man here.

00:46:11.040 --> 00:46:12.780
Did you ever see him before?

00:46:12.780 --> 00:46:16.050
- Yes. - When?

00:46:16.050 --> 00:46:19.770
The gentleman was here earlier tonight.

00:46:19.770 --> 00:46:20.660
Alone?

00:46:20.660 --> 00:46:24.110
No, he was with the lady.

00:46:24.110 --> 00:46:26.260
Did he buy anything?

00:46:26.260 --> 00:46:28.640
Silk handkerchief for the lady.

00:46:28.640 --> 00:46:29.570
That all?

00:46:30.700 --> 00:46:33.420
The gentleman also bought a knife.

00:46:33.420 --> 00:46:34.420
What kind of knife?

00:46:34.420 --> 00:46:37.500
A knife with a jade handle.

00:46:37.500 --> 00:46:38.520
Got lettuce.

00:46:38.520 --> 00:46:40.010
Got fruit.

00:46:40.010 --> 00:46:41.010
To hang on the wall, maybe?

00:46:41.010 --> 00:46:43.280
Describe the jade handle.

00:46:43.280 --> 00:46:45.900
The jade handle had a curved monkey.

00:46:45.900 --> 00:46:47.820
We know that. Describe the monkey.

00:46:47.820 --> 00:46:50.130
Monkey was holding his eyes.

00:46:50.130 --> 00:46:53.690
So.

00:46:53.690 --> 00:46:54.690
You're crazy.

00:46:54.690 --> 00:46:56.840
I bought the one that was holding his ears.

00:46:56.840 --> 00:46:59.510
The gentleman is mistaken.

00:47:00.760 --> 00:47:03.760
Are you sure the one he bought was holding its size?

00:47:03.760 --> 00:47:05.550
They completed a set.

00:47:05.550 --> 00:47:07.720
First one is sold to this gentleman.

00:47:07.720 --> 00:47:09.270
The others I still have.

00:47:09.270 --> 00:47:11.090
I can show you.

00:47:11.090 --> 00:47:11.940
Show me.

00:47:11.940 --> 00:47:21.800
These are imported from Hong Kong.

00:47:21.800 --> 00:47:23.800
I only ordered one set.

00:47:23.800 --> 00:47:26.040
Costs too much.

00:47:26.040 --> 00:47:28.130
Never sold any except to this gentleman.

00:47:30.320 --> 00:47:30.820
See?

00:47:33.570 --> 00:47:37.420
Well, Mr. Scott?

00:47:38.860 --> 00:47:45.890
I don't understand. I'm sure I bought this one.

00:47:47.230 --> 00:47:48.430
The one that's holding its ears.

00:47:48.430 --> 00:47:49.630
Why did you buy any knife?

00:47:49.630 --> 00:47:50.430
I didn't buy a knife.

00:47:51.160 --> 00:47:53.090
I mean, I didn't intend to buy a knife, but...

00:47:53.800 --> 00:47:56.800
Lorna was looking for Jade, and she said the only Jade she had was on the knife handles.

00:47:58.300 --> 00:47:59.860
And the one we finally bought was this one.

00:48:01.240 --> 00:48:05.600
- The one that's holding its ears? - Perhaps Madame Chin switched to the knives, huh?

00:48:05.600 --> 00:48:11.880
- She must have. - Did you ever sit Chin before?

00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:18.120
- No. - Then why would she change the knives?

00:48:34.920 --> 00:48:36.420
Why would you change the knives?

00:48:36.420 --> 00:48:40.920
I don't know.

00:48:40.920 --> 00:48:46.660
Because you are a stranger, and only because you are a stranger,

00:48:46.660 --> 00:48:49.540
we've given you every chance to clear yourself.

00:48:49.540 --> 00:48:53.680
You should have been locked up an hour ago.

00:48:53.680 --> 00:48:55.210
Admit it.

00:48:55.210 --> 00:48:56.820
You know you killed her.

00:49:01.210 --> 00:49:02.120
Admit it!

00:49:02.120 --> 00:49:08.010
All right.

00:49:08.010 --> 00:49:09.010
Then you did kill her?

00:49:09.010 --> 00:49:12.450
Yes.

00:49:12.450 --> 00:49:14.080
Why, Mr. Scott?

00:49:14.080 --> 00:49:23.570
Because she was afraid.

00:49:23.570 --> 00:49:24.570
Because she wanted to go back.

00:49:24.570 --> 00:49:25.630
Back?

00:49:25.630 --> 00:49:27.030
Where?

00:49:27.030 --> 00:49:27.950
To her husband.

00:49:27.950 --> 00:49:29.550
Her husband?

00:49:29.550 --> 00:49:30.000
Her name wasn't.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:35.430
and Mrs. Scott, her name was Mrs. Eddie Roman.

00:49:35.430 --> 00:49:37.900
We left Miami together last night on the Cuba.

00:49:37.900 --> 00:49:39.800
We docked here this morning.

00:49:39.800 --> 00:49:41.040
Didn't leave our cabin until it was dark.

00:49:41.040 --> 00:49:45.320
We wound up in that nightclub.

00:49:45.320 --> 00:49:51.750
We had a drink there.

00:49:51.750 --> 00:49:57.910
- Mr. Scott, you are a gentleman.

00:49:57.910 --> 00:50:00.000
Only from the viewpoint of the police, of course.

00:50:02.040 --> 00:50:02.720
I'll see you there.

00:51:00.510 --> 00:51:01.510
Just a moment.

00:51:04.020 --> 00:51:07.680
- Did you see his name? - Yes, he climbed all the way up to the floor.

00:51:07.780 --> 00:51:09.560
- Up there! - Get over here.

00:51:09.660 --> 00:51:10.760
Very well, boss.

00:51:15.040 --> 00:51:26.280
- Get out of the way. - He's a good guy.

00:52:03.610 --> 00:52:04.070
Thank you.

00:52:44.140 --> 00:52:46.140
He has to be in the building, there are no signs of the band.

00:52:46.140 --> 00:52:48.140
How could he have escaped from the emergency room?

00:52:48.140 --> 00:52:50.000
They are looking for all the rooms.

00:52:50.000 --> 00:52:51.890
And this room, what are we going to do with it?

00:52:51.890 --> 00:52:53.890
He must be here in this building.

00:52:53.890 --> 00:52:54.840
We are going to look for him, he has to be in here.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.980
It's the door, it's the authority!

00:53:02.980 --> 00:53:06.240
Open the door!

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:09.540
Go ahead!

00:53:09.540 --> 00:53:13.360
There's no business here in my house, you know?

00:53:13.360 --> 00:53:14.520
Don't call me, I take the cart!

00:53:14.520 --> 00:53:15.520
Don't call me anything!

00:53:15.520 --> 00:53:17.540
It's in this building, let's go.

00:53:17.540 --> 00:53:19.260
Yes, it's in the building, we'll find it.

00:53:19.260 --> 00:53:20.100
I'm sure, let's go!

00:53:20.100 --> 00:53:24.610
Soon!

00:53:32.520 --> 00:53:34.270
Thanks a lot.

00:53:34.270 --> 00:53:43.960
Say, you, uh, you never saw me before, but you helped me.

00:53:43.960 --> 00:53:47.010
Why?

00:53:47.010 --> 00:53:48.980
Cups.

00:53:48.980 --> 00:53:49.980
I hate cups.

00:53:49.980 --> 00:53:56.860
Is there, uh, any other way out of here?

00:53:56.860 --> 00:53:59.030
Only the way you came in.

00:54:00.570 --> 00:54:01.350
Are you kind of?

00:54:02.640 --> 00:54:02.990
Yeah.

00:54:04.150 --> 00:54:04.790
Yeah, I'm an American.

00:54:06.350 --> 00:54:07.350
Miss, I just thought of something.

00:54:08.370 --> 00:54:10.530
Do you know the man that takes the pictures at the La Habana Club?

00:54:10.610 --> 00:54:12.240
You know the, uh, flashlights photographs?

00:54:13.400 --> 00:54:18.130
It's not that it matters now, but I just thought that maybe he did get something.

00:54:18.690 --> 00:54:21.090
And if he did, it might...

00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:19.560
Happy?

00:56:11.840 --> 00:56:13.180
- No, no, no, no.

00:56:13.180 --> 00:56:16.310
No, no.

00:56:16.310 --> 00:56:18.670
We pay you the same as we paid the last time

00:56:18.670 --> 00:56:20.700
and not one cent more.

00:56:20.700 --> 00:56:23.200
- Then perhaps I do business elsewhere.

00:56:23.200 --> 00:56:25.520
- Look, we run the stuff across, not you.

00:56:25.520 --> 00:56:28.600
What do you have to do, just wear out that seat?

00:56:28.600 --> 00:56:29.700
- Of course that you do.

00:56:30.090 --> 00:56:34.130
I don't mind assuming the usual business risks, but when it comes to knifing women...

00:56:34.130 --> 00:56:37.880
Knifing women? All you did is switch a couple of knives.

00:56:37.880 --> 00:56:43.290
I had a visit from the police tonight. They asked a lot of questions.

00:56:43.290 --> 00:56:46.870
In our business, you can't afford visits from the police.

00:58:30.030 --> 00:58:33.640
No deal.

00:58:33.640 --> 00:58:34.500
No?

00:58:34.500 --> 00:58:36.590
Then you're out of business.

00:58:36.590 --> 00:58:37.590
I don't think so.

00:58:37.590 --> 00:58:40.630
Who's going to buy your stuff?

00:58:40.630 --> 00:58:41.610
You are.

00:58:41.610 --> 00:58:42.730
Yeah?

00:58:42.730 --> 00:58:44.070
Why?

00:58:44.070 --> 00:58:51.840
If you don't, certain people may find out certain things which you might not want mentioned.

00:58:51.840 --> 00:58:54.560
I'm sorry you said that.

00:58:54.560 --> 00:58:57.870
I'm sorry it has to be said.

01:00:37.960 --> 01:00:45.560
- I could never make it, I could never make it.

01:02:30.800 --> 01:02:33.970
- Naval Hospital.

01:02:33.970 --> 01:02:36.750
Commander Davidson, just a moment, please.

01:02:36.750 --> 01:02:39.100
Commander Davidson's office.

01:02:39.100 --> 01:02:40.570
Who?

01:02:40.570 --> 01:02:43.420
Oh, of course I remember you, Scott.

01:02:43.420 --> 01:02:45.370
Yes, he's here.

01:02:45.370 --> 01:02:52.840
Of course you may, just a minute.

01:02:52.840 --> 01:02:54.780
Chuck Scott would like to speak to you, sir.

01:02:54.780 --> 01:02:56.300
- Fine. - He's on the phone.

01:02:56.300 --> 01:02:58.060
- Oh.

01:02:58.060 --> 01:02:59.350
- Hello, Chuck.

01:03:00.060 --> 01:03:03.080
You said if I ever needed you, I could call?

01:03:04.920 --> 01:03:06.440
Oh, I need you now.

01:03:07.750 --> 01:03:08.640
Yes, sir.

01:03:11.820 --> 01:03:13.380
Well, it's happened again.

01:03:14.520 --> 01:03:15.520
Yes, sir.

01:03:16.700 --> 01:03:17.910
Yes, sir.

01:03:20.170 --> 01:03:22.740
I'll be there as soon as I get there.

01:03:23.410 --> 01:03:24.260
Thanks, sir.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:30.800
Get easy Chuck.

01:03:32.750 --> 01:03:34.650
Now let's try and start with the beginning.

01:03:37.690 --> 01:03:39.090
There doesn't seem to be any beginning.

01:03:40.850 --> 01:03:45.080
All I can remember is the end of it.

01:03:51.660 --> 01:03:55.350
Sit down Chuck.

01:04:03.770 --> 01:04:12.680
his outfit. Where'd I get this uniform? In the room I woke up in. How'd I get in that

01:04:12.680 --> 01:04:20.450
house? Let's talk about what you remember. Forget about the uniform. Well, yes, I was

01:04:20.450 --> 01:04:28.300
running away from the police in Havana, in the middle of the night. Chuck, you haven't

01:04:28.300 --> 01:04:30.000
been to Havana in three or four years to mind.

01:04:31.340 --> 01:04:32.500
So we can eliminate that.

01:04:32.860 --> 01:04:33.680
That's dream stuff.

01:04:35.250 --> 01:04:38.280
But the girl that you met here in Miami, that's real.

01:04:39.070 --> 01:04:40.890
The girl that you drove to the beach.

01:04:41.520 --> 01:04:44.390
The one that wanted to know what's out there straight ahead.

01:04:45.920 --> 01:04:46.460
That girl.

01:04:50.150 --> 01:04:54.650
Yes, but that's all I remember.

01:04:55.230 --> 01:04:56.480
What she said.

01:04:58.210 --> 01:05:00.000
But the beach, you said you remember the beach.

01:05:01.820 --> 01:05:02.660
Yeah, the beach.

01:05:04.080 --> 01:05:05.610
But that's all.

01:05:07.490 --> 01:05:08.810
Why do you keep looking at the clock?

01:05:09.960 --> 01:05:12.000
I don't know, Doc.

01:05:12.810 --> 01:05:17.210
I keep feeling that there's something that I've got to do.

01:05:18.490 --> 01:05:19.370
Don't let that worry you.

01:05:20.330 --> 01:05:21.810
That's symptomatic in shock cases.

01:05:23.160 --> 01:05:24.540
But you did remember to call me.

01:05:25.350 --> 01:05:26.570
You did remember to come here.

01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:29.250
You're pretty well out of a check.

01:05:33.160 --> 01:05:34.400
Yes, but I keep feeling that I...

01:05:34.400 --> 01:05:34.780
I know.

01:05:35.860 --> 01:05:41.610
Technically, this would be identified, in a case such as yours, as an anxiety neurosis.

01:05:43.010 --> 01:05:44.210
That sounds terrible, doesn't it?

01:05:44.860 --> 01:05:46.240
But it's not, Chuck.

01:05:47.050 --> 01:05:47.970
Believe me, it's not.

01:05:49.580 --> 01:05:50.040
You understand?

01:05:52.010 --> 01:05:53.170
Yes, sir.

01:05:57.600 --> 01:05:59.350
I still keep feeling that I've...

01:06:10.360 --> 01:06:18.780
I'll be waiting in my room.

01:06:18.780 --> 01:06:20.360
See you later.

01:06:31.440 --> 01:06:32.200
Be happy, Lorna.

01:06:32.750 --> 01:06:34.450
We're going to have fun tonight.

01:06:35.470 --> 01:06:36.110
I'm going to take you out.

01:06:36.880 --> 01:06:38.240
We'll go to the Florida Club.

01:06:39.270 --> 01:06:40.510
Would you rather go for a ride?

01:06:41.310 --> 01:06:42.700
Take a look at the ocean.

01:06:44.700 --> 01:06:46.980
Scotty showed me a rendezvous this afternoon.

01:06:48.710 --> 01:06:49.510
Got a very nice view.

01:06:49.780 --> 01:07:00.000
Very nervous this evening, Lorna.

01:07:00.990 --> 01:07:02.520
What's the matter?

01:07:02.520 --> 01:07:04.080
Job.

01:07:04.080 --> 01:07:06.080
Will you please tell Scotty to bring the car around?

01:07:06.080 --> 01:07:08.700
Scotty's gone.

01:07:08.700 --> 01:07:12.530
Go.

01:07:12.530 --> 01:07:14.470
Yeah, quit.

01:07:14.470 --> 01:07:16.090
He saw him leave.

01:07:16.090 --> 01:07:18.100
He even yelled after him.

01:07:18.100 --> 01:07:19.990
Didn't even turn around.

01:07:19.990 --> 01:07:23.520
It's going to cost you 125 bucks for a new uniform.

01:07:23.520 --> 01:07:29.240
Still want to go for that ride?

01:07:29.240 --> 01:07:30.000
Thanks.

01:07:48.970 --> 01:07:49.970
Good evening, Commander.

01:07:49.970 --> 01:07:54.600
Good evening, Ben.

01:07:54.600 --> 01:07:55.600
